  "id": "Compound::DB01403 - Gene::151",
  "verbalization": "Methotrimeprazine is likely to interact with Adra2b through a shared pathway involving alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Methotrimeprazine binds to Adra2c, which then participates in alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately being participated by Adra2b. This indicates a potential mechanism where Methotrimeprazine influences the activity of Adra2b via Adra2c, possibly through a common intermediate in the alpha-adrenergic signaling cascade. The consistent binding to Adra2c and the participation in alpha-adrenergic activity across multiple paths support a unified mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction between Methotrimeprazine and Adra2c remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence highlights a recurring link between Methotrimeprazine and alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, suggesting a broader role in the pharmacological effects of the drug.",
